  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), Friday 15 January 1904, for the places of the members elected in 1901 (Wake, J. McNeice, Fleming, Douie and Maxwell Thompson). \"Of some 2400 electors on the register 1477 voted\", a falling-off of almost 200 on 1903 put down to the severity of the day; declared at 10.30 p.m. The spoiled papers are not given. No party labels printed. William White: no party label printed in 1904. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Lurgan, Armagh County Council, 28 May 1902, printed 'U': Armagh Guardian, 2 May 1902, p. 2 (\"But Few Contests\": county council nominations, with labels); members confirmed by the Lurgan Times, 7 June 1902, p. 3 (\"Armagh County Council\": complete list of the elected members); Lurgan, Armagh County Council, 25 May 1905, printed 'U': Armagh Guardian, 28 April 1905, p. 5 (\"Nominations: County Councillors\")). Joshua McNeice: no party label printed in 1904. At other elections he stood as Labour (Lurgan, 16 January 1899, listed as Labour: Belfast News-Letter, 18 January 1899, p. 7 (\"Urban District Councils\"); Lurgan, 15 January 1912, printed 'L.': Lurgan Mail, 20 January 1912, p. 5 (\"The Municipal Election: A Heavy Poll\"); labels from the Lurgan Times, 20 January 1912, p. 2 (\"Monday's Election\"))."
